th tones we  have tones and other tones and so we  have intonation in Chinese they have  intonation but it determines the meaning  of a word when you learn vocabulary and  if you're learning an opinion and even  on my old cards here they would have a  marker for the tones like she okay UN  and so there's four tones  ma ma ma ma the fourth is a falling tone  and this is again described on that  chinesepod webpage and there are funny  rules like you know if you've got 2/3  tone mama it's active ma ma so you have  to learn that and sometimes a rising  tone becomes or at least the falling  tone becomes alright there's a few rules  there go and look at them but in the end  you won't be able to remember the rules  that well you won't be able to remember  that well the individual tones of the  characters you have to get used to  hearing them in combination learning  them as phrases just as we do in any  language and in that regard I found  listening to Chinese comic dialogue I  was going to show you some example here  we are yung-chun of which I have many  many many at home these are the best  because they sang strong performers tend  to exaggerate and you have to exaggerate  the intonation try to imitate that  intonation and if you do that you will  get the tones and you will get a natural  flow to the language but it means a lot  of listening and I would put the  emphasis on initially getting started  with opinion seeing how the pinyin works  some of its idiosyncrasies and then just  listening to a lot listening of course  to material that you understand because  it's very frustrating to listen to  things that you don't understand so  listen and read save words get to our  you understand certain things then  listen to it over and over again so that  some of these phrases become almost like  you know Buddhist chants in your brain  like your brain is really starting to  get the rhythm of the tones and if you  put effort into doing that then you will  conquer the mysteries of Mandarin  Chinese pronunciation but you won't be  perfect and you needn't strive for  perfection but you can strive for  constant improvement that's all I have  for you today bye for now  [Music]
 

